<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Mac App Store entitlements for the embedded Briefcase Python engine
  ("Fichero Engine.app"), the nested helper inside the MAS app bundle (#3748).

  Distinct from FicheroEngine.entitlements, which is the DMG / Developer ID
  channel: that file carries four com.apple.security.cs.* keys, which are
  HARDENED-RUNTIME exceptions required by notarization. The MAS build does not
  go through notarization, and the sandbox spike (#3746) proved empirically that
  the real 1.0 GB engine — 2,889 native libs mapped, incl. duckdb / numpy /
  onnxruntime / lance / pyarrow — loads with NO hardened runtime and NO cs.* keys
  at all. So they are not merely unnecessary here; they must not be added back on
  a hunch.

  EXACTLY TWO KEYS. This is a hard rule, not a minimalism preference: per Apple's
  Entitlement Key Reference, com.apple.security.inherit is incompatible with any
  OTHER App Sandbox key, and the system ABORTS the child if one is present. The
  child inherits the parent's sandbox — that is where network.server (loopback
  bind) and user-selected file access come from. Do not add keys to this file.

  Two things this file cannot do by itself:
  - CODE_SIGN_INJECT_BASE_ENTITLEMENTS must be NO wherever the helper is signed:
    Xcode's injected get-task-allow is itself an "other key" and breaks inherit.
    The engine is signed by the "Embed Fichero Engine" phase, which passes this
    file explicitly to codesign, so nothing is injected.

  (Note for editors: this is an XML comment, so it may not contain a double
  hyphen. plutil tolerates one; a strict XML parser does not.)
  - Sandbox inheritance passes only STATIC rights. The Powerbox grant the user
    makes in NSOpenPanel is dynamic and is NOT inherited, so the engine still
    cannot open a library outside the container without security-scoped bookmark
    plumbing (#3747).
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>com.apple.security.app-sandbox</key>
	<true/>
	<key>com.apple.security.inherit</key>
	<true/>
</dict>
</plist>
